implementationPlan.description:
DoD 3 + 4 — PROVE THE SEMANTICS ARE UNCHANGED AND THE GATE IS GREEN.

(a) Run the focused gate standalone, foreground and unpiped, and quote the count line:
`pnpm --filter @moe/daemon exec vitest run --root . --config package.json src/orchestrator/agent-wrapper.test.ts src/orchestrator/verifier-process-runner.test.ts src/orchestrator/agent-wrapper-main.test.ts src/orchestrator/wrapper-knobs.test.ts`
ARCHITECT MEASURED: **Test Files 4 passed (4), Tests 85 passed (85)**. **THE PARK'S '4 files/81 tests' IS STALE** — the count moved to 85 when main's merge added arms. Record 85 with that explanation; do not chase 81 and do not read the delta as a regression. (The two owned test files alone are 2 files / 61 tests.)
Then run `pnpm --filter @moe/daemon typecheck` and require exit 0 with its `$ tsc` echo. Read the OUTPUT, not the exit code — 'No test files found' and 'No projects matched the filters' both exit 0.

(b) DoD 3, verified rather than assumed. An extraction most easily breaks ORDERING while every test stays green, so check these specifically:
  - public and bin surface unchanged (compare the export lists and the bin entries);
  - spawn argv unchanged, element for element;
  - cancellation and cleanup ORDERING unchanged — verify with a call-order recorder asserting position(a) < position(b), not by reading the code;
  - output-tail bounds unchanged;
  - exact refusal code AND layer unchanged on every transition.
  Confirm error-path cleanup is exercised (DoD 4 names it), not just the success path.

(c) Record the full daemon lane as a merge-base-versus-HEAD path-attributed baseline; the delta intersected with the owned paths must be EMPTY, and any foreign red is disclosed verbatim.
